## Overview

`TxPhysicsMotion` preserves every named non-loader whimsical implementation as its own scene. Paper folds use actual hinged layers and clipping; stroke scenes retain their original SVG coordinates; mechanical scenes retain their own pivot, motion vector, scale sequence and phase offsets. `TxMotionDock` owns the separate caller-driven dock. The CSS loaders and UI-kit controls are documented under their own components.

Artwork has an explicit assembled pose. Pausing, disabling, leaving the viewport, hiding the document, KeepAlive deactivation or reduced motion cancels native animations and timers, revealing that readable pose. Decorative playback does not announce or simulate business completion.

Grab the scene and throw it: the artwork follows the pointer 1:1 from the point you grabbed and springs back with the velocity of the release, while its choreography keeps playing. With reduced motion the artwork still follows the pointer and then jumps back.

## Usage

### Complete catalogue

The demo renders all 61 named scenes, filters by original ID or symbol, and provides a keyboard-operable trigger on every specimen. The selected scene additionally exposes trigger, loop, speed, content and replay controls.

:::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="PhysicsMotionDemo" code-lang="vue"}
---
code: |
  <script setup lang="ts">
  import { ref } from 'vue'
  const replayKey = ref(0)
  </script>

  <template>
    <TxButton @click="replayKey++">Replay</TxButton>
    <TxPhysicsMotion
      variant="anim-origami-envelope"
      trigger="click"
      :loop="false"
      :replay-key="replayKey"
      :labels="{ replay: 'Replay envelope', content: 'Preview' }"
    >
      Envelope preview
    </TxPhysicsMotion>
  </template>
---
:::

### Playback and triggers

`auto` starts when the artwork becomes visible. `hover` supplies pointer-entry and focus replay; `click` supplies native button activation, including Enter and Space. `manual` starts only through `replay()` or a changed `replayKey`. A replay interrupts and replaces the previous choreography without forcing a reflow.

`loop=true` retains the upstream automatic repeating preview, including for hover/click scenes. Use `loop=false` for a strictly input-triggered one-shot. Each scene restarts at its original `useLoopFlg` cadence; tracks with a distinct duration keep that duration, such as the one-second metronome or four-second gear tracks. A one-shot completes its longest track and then shows the assembled pose.

### Dragging

Press the stage and move 4 px to pick the scene up: the artwork lifts to 1.04× and follows the pointer 1:1 from the point you grabbed, while its choreography keeps playing. It can travel as far as the edges of its stage; beyond them a rubber band holds it. On release the scene inherits the pointer's velocity over the last 100ms and springs home. A release that carried speed swings past home with a damping ratio near 0.8, a slow one settles without bounce. There is a single place to rest, so nothing is projected from the release.

Grabbing the scene again while it is returning continues from where it is drawn. Escape, or a cancelled pointer, sends it home without overshoot. A drag never replays the scene: only a click, Enter or Space does. A `paused` scene can still be thrown; a `disabled` one cannot. The stage declares `touch-action: pan-y`, and a touch that sets off vertically scrolls the page instead of picking the scene up.

## API Reference

### Props

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `variant` | `PhysicsMotionVariant` | `'anim-card-peel'` | Exact ID from the source mapping below. |
| `trigger` | `'auto' \| 'hover' \| 'click' \| 'manual'` | `'auto'` | Automatic visibility playback, input replay or API-only playback. |
| `loop` | `boolean` | `true` | Retain the scene's own restart cadence and internal track durations. |
| `paused` | `boolean` | `false` | Cancel playback and reveal the assembled pose. A queued replay can start on resume. |
| `disabled` | `boolean` | `false` | Stop animation, disable dragging and the native interactive stage. |
| `draggable` | `boolean` | `true` | Grab the scene and throw it; it springs home with the release's velocity. Replays by click, Enter, Space or the API are unaffected; `false` leaves pointer drags to the host. |
| `replayKey` | `string \| number` | — | Changing the key requests another run without remounting. |
| `speed` | `number` | `1` | Playback multiplier, clamped to 0.1–5; non-finite values use 1. |
| `size` | `'xs' \| 'sm' \| 'md' \| 'lg'` | `'md'` | 96, 128, 160 or 192px stage, with proportionally scaled geometry. |
| `ariaLabel` | `string` | Source symbol or `labels.replay` | Accessible name; hover/click stages are native buttons, others are images. |
| `labels` | `Partial<PhysicsMotionLabels>` | See below | Localized action and artwork content. |

#### Labels

| Key | Default | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `replay` | `'Replay animation'` | Default accessible name of interactive stages. |
| `content` | `'Open'` | Actual revealed text in the gate and sliding shutter. |
| `north` | `'N'` | North dipole block label. |
| `south` | `'S'` | South dipole block label. |

### Events

| Event | Payload | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `play` | `PhysicsMotionVariant` | An actual native playback or source-loop restart starts. |
| `finish` | `PhysicsMotionVariant` | The longest one-shot track finishes; the assembled pose is visible. Looping or cancellation does not emit this event. |
| `covered` | `PhysicsMotionVariant` | Tsumiki's actual 1400ms source milestone, adjusted by speed. It is not a save, navigation or network result. |

### Slots and methods

| Entry | Contract |
| --- | --- |
| `default` slot | Optional caption outside the interactive stage, associated through a stable Vue ID. |
| `replay()` | Replace the current run. If inactive, retain the request until active; reduced motion keeps the assembled pose. |
| `reset()` | Cancel all tracks and queued replay, revealing the assembled pose. |
| `playing` | Exposed boolean indicating that real native tracks are currently owned by this instance. |

### Exports

`TxPhysicsMotion`, installable `PhysicsMotion`, `TxPhysicsMotionInstance`, `PhysicsMotionProps`, `PhysicsMotionEmits`, `PhysicsMotionLabels`, `PhysicsMotionTrigger`, `PhysicsMotionVariant` and `PhysicsMotionSource` are exported from `@talex-touch/tuffex/physics-motion`.

`PHYSICS_MOTION_VARIANTS` is the complete readonly ID tuple. `PHYSICS_MOTION_SOURCES` contains one real mapping per variant with `variant`, `symbol`, `file`, `period` and `behavior`. `PHYSICS_MOTION_DEFAULT_LABELS` supplies the defaults above.

### CSS variables

| Variable | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `--tx-physics-accent` | Optional scene accent; otherwise uses `--tx-color-primary`. Related tones mix that accent with the host's surface and ink tokens. |
| `--tx-physics-size` / `--tx-physics-scale` | Stage length and dimensionless artwork scale, driven together by `size`. |

All paper, line, background and text colors use the host's `--tx-*` tokens. Hover color changes are immediate.

